Chinese director Zou Jing&#x2019;s A Girl Unknown won the top $75,000 Best Narrative prize at the Doha Film Festival as the second edition of its revamped format came to a close on Friday evening.

The China-set first feature follows the fate of a young girl who is found abandoned as a baby in a rubbish bin and then grows up from babyhood through to adolescence with three sets of different guardians and circumstances.

The film world premiered in Cannes Critics&#x2019; Week earlier this year where it won the Fipresci Prize. Related Stories News International Insider: Doha Days; Tricky Week For BAFTA; 'Remarried Empress' Interview News Todd Boehly Dissects How Daniel Katz's Trading Desk Acumen Fed Into A24 Success: "Very Few Entertainment People Understand Math"

