Best Actress was awarded posthumously Josette Kwanya for her performance in House of the Wind as an elderly Cameroonian woman waiting for her children to return home after they left for Europe in search of opportunities in Europe.

This year&#x2019;s jury was presided over by Japanese director Naomi Kawase, who was joined by by Oscar-winning documentarian Gianfranco Rosi, rising actor Adam Bessa, Tunisian producer Dora Bouchoucha and Palestinian director Kamal Aljafari.

In further prizes, Best Documentary went to Asmahan Bkerat &#x2019; s Concrete Land about a Bedouin family struggling to preserve their traditional way of life in tents, as well as the Fipresci prize, which is being awarded at the festival for the first time this year.

In further documentary prizes, Tala Hadid&#x2019;s Bardi won the Best Artistic Achievement for Documentary.

Fatma Hassan Alremaihi, Festival Director and CEO of Doha Film Institute said the 2026 Doha Film Festival tapped into her institute's belief in &#x201C;the power of stories to transcend borders, challenge perspectives and bring the experiences of people and communities into the global conversation.&#x201D;

&#x201C;At Doha Film Institute, we believe that important voices deserve to be seen, heard and recognised. Doha Film Festival exists to provide that platform, bringing together filmmakers and audiences from across the world, championing bold and independent storytelling, and creating space for stories that might otherwise go untold,&#x201D; she said. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

